## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to bridge native platform APIs with React Native, implement real-time peer-to-peer networking, and manage data flow under mobile network constraints.

## Key Concepts
- WebRTC Data Channels and binary message handling
- TurboModules and the JSI bridge for high-performance native interop
- NAT traversal using ICE, STUN, and TURN servers
- DTLS encryption for secure data transmission
- Backpressure management and binary framing protocols

## Code Example
```javascript
// Initialize the WebRTC data channel
await RNWebRTC.initConnection({
  iceServers: [
    { urls: 'stun:stun.l.google.com:19302' },
    { urls: 'turn:your-turn-server.com', username: 'user', credential: 'pass' }
  ],
  peerId: 'technician-device-001'
});

// Listen for incoming messages
RNWebRTC.onMessage((event) => {
  const { data } = event;
  console.log('Received:', data);
});

// Send binary telemetry
await RNWebRTC.sendMessage({ type: 'telemetry', payload: sensorData });

// Clean up when done
await RNWebRTC.closeConnection();
```

